</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our work, while illuminating the critical role of the first reasoning step in the chain-of-thought processes of LLMs, possesses several limitations. First, our empirical evaluations primarily focus on mathematical and scientific reasoning tasks. Thus, the findings regarding the significance of first reasoning steps and the effectiveness of our pruning strategy may not directly generalize to broader domains such as code writing, commonsense reasoning, or creative writing tasks. Despite this limitation, our method possesses inherent flexibility and can potentially generalize or adapt to new scenarios with suitable modifications or training adjustments. Second, our proposed early pruning method relies on a process reward model (PRM) trained specifically on mathematical reasoning datasets, limiting its applicability to contexts where high-quality reward models are unavailable or challenging to develop. Lastly, the LaBoR benchmark specifically targets mathematical reasoning tasks and consists of a relatively small number of samples, potentially limiting the generalizability of our findings. However, the automated pipeline we propose makes it feasible to extend the benchmark to new domains or larger datasets.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Boarder impacts</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work identifies a critical vulnerability in LLMs: the disproportionate influence of the first reasoning step on the final output during long CoT reasoning. Our findings reveal that even minor early mistakes can drastically degrade model performance, and that current models have limited capacity for self-correction. To address this, we introduce a dual contribution: (1) a lightweight early pruning method that discards unpromising initial reasoning paths, reducing inference cost while preserving accuracy; and (2) LaBoR, a benchmark specifically designed to evaluate models’ self-correction abilities in the presence of flawed first steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our method directly improves the efficiency and robustness of LLMs, two crucial goals for scaling their deployment. The proposed early pruning mechanism can reduce inference cost by up to 70% without performance degradation, contributing to the sustainability of LLM use.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, the LaBoR benchmark enables more rigorous evaluation of a model’s reasoning capabilities, especially its ability to self-correct—a key desideratum for safe deployment in high-stakes domains such as education, law, and scientific discovery. By spotlighting the limitations of current models, this work encourages the development of reasoning architectures that are more trustworthy and interpretable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">There are also risks. Efficiency improvements may lower the barrier to misuse—enabling broader deployment of LLMs in contexts where safety mechanisms are underdeveloped (e.g., disinformation generation or rapid, low-cost model abuse). The benchmark, while designed for rigorous evaluation, could potentially be reverse-engineered as an adversarial testbed to construct prompts that reliably induce reasoning failures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">More broadly, this work underscores a weakness in LLM reasoning—namely, overreliance on initial cues—which may deepen existing user trust in model outputs without fully addressing reliability. If misinterpreted, this may create a false sense of security in self-correction capabilities and lead to blind adoption in sensitive workflows.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>LaBoR data</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Please refer to the supplementary material for the data file.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Semantic similarity between first reasoning step and final answer</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also report the cosine similarity between the embedding of the <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th reasoning step <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the final conclusion <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, interpolated using the average number of reasoning steps (Figure <a href="#A4.F1" title="Figure D.1 ‣ Appendix D Semantic similarity between first reasoning step and final answer ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left</span>). To mitigate the influence of varying text lengths across reasoning steps, we additionally segment the thinking context into fixed-length chunks, where each chunk has the same length as the first reasoning step. As shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F1" title="Figure D.1 ‣ Appendix D Semantic similarity between first reasoning step and final answer ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, the high semantic similarity between the first reasoning step and the final answer remains consistent.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F1.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v1/semantic_similarity_plot_mean.svg" id="A4.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/333;" width="476" height="333"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F1.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v1/semantic_similarity_plot_longest_token.svg" id="A4.F1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/333;" width="476" height="333"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F1.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v1/semantic_similarity_plot_mean_token.svg" id="A4.F1.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/333;" width="476" height="333"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure D.1</span>: </span><span id="A4.F1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Cosine similarity between the embedding of the <math id="A4.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th reasoning step <math id="A4.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the final conclusion <math id="A4.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, interpolated using the average number of reasoning steps <span id="A4.F1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Left)</span>. Cosine similarity between the embedding of the <math id="A4.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th span <math id="A4.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, interpolated using the maximum number of split chunks <span id="A4.F1.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Middle)</span> or the average number of reasoning steps <span id="A4.F1.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Right)</span>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Examples for minor perturbation</h2>

<figure id="A5.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="260.72" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 260.72" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,260.72) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 254.81 C 0 258.07 2.64 260.72 5.91 260.72 L 471.47 260.72 C 474.73 260.72 477.38 258.07 477.38 254.81 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E8EEF7;" fill="#E8EEF7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 236.6 L 475.41 236.6 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 245.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Original final conclusion</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 33.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.91em;--ltx-fo-height:13.83em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.43em;font-size:10pt;" height="211.02" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 191.3)" width="469.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.91em;">
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we are given triangle <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> with side lengths <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…]</span></span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Compute <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies on line segment <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the circle, the point <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2025</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a common denominator:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4225</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4225</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2025</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2200</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Step: Compute <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+n</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The reduced form of <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.F1.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100}{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100}{13}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100,\hskip 9.24994ptn=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{\textbackslash boxed\lx@text@lbrace 113\lx@text@rbrace}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#FF8000" mathsize="0.900em">\boxed{113}</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100,\hskip 9.24994ptn=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{\textbackslash boxed\lx@text@lbrace 113\lx@text@rbrace}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">Final Answer: <span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">\boxed{113}</span><span id="A5.F1.pic1.2.6.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.F1.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="224.12" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 224.12" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,224.12) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 218.22 C 0 221.48 2.64 224.12 5.91 224.12 L 471.47 224.12 C 474.73 224.12 477.38 221.48 477.38 218.22 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DDEAF6;" fill="#DDEAF6" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 202.7 L 475.41 202.7 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 208.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">New correct first reason</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.91em;--ltx-fo-height:12.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="177.12" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 174.69)" width="469.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.91em;">
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we are given triangle <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> with side lengths <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…]</span></span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Compute <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies on line segment <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the circle, the point <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2025</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a common denominator:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4225</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4225</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2025</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2200</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic2.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Step: Compute <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+n</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The reduced form of <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.F1.pic2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100}{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100}{13}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100,\hskip 9.24994ptn=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{113}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#FF8000" mathsize="0.900em">113</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100,\hskip 9.24994ptn=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{113}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.F1.pic3" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="224.12" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 224.12" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,224.12) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 218.22 C 0 221.48 2.64 224.12 5.91 224.12 L 471.47 224.12 C 474.73 224.12 477.38 221.48 477.38 218.22 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FDF0E6;" fill="#FDF0E6" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 202.7 L 475.41 202.7 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 208.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">New incorrect first reason</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.91em;--ltx-fo-height:12.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="177.12" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 174.69)" width="469.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.91em;">
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To solve the problem, we are given triangle <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABC</annotation></semantics></math> with side lengths <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC=9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…]</span></span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Compute <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies on line segment <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies outside the circle, the point <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2025</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP=DA-DP=\frac{325}{22}-\frac{2025}{286}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a common denominator:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">325</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">22</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4225</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4225</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2025</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2200</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">286</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{325}{22}=\frac{4225}{286}\Rightarrow AP=\frac{4225-2025}{286}=\frac{2200}{286}=\frac{100}{13}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F1.pic3.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Step: Compute <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+n</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The reduced form of <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AP</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.F1.pic3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{100}{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{100}{13}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100,\hskip 9.24994ptn=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{103}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#FF8000" mathsize="0.900em">103</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100,\hskip 9.24994ptn=13\Rightarrow m+n={\color[rgb]{1,0.5,0}\text{{103}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure E.1</span>: </span><span id="A5.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of a targeted perturbation to create correct and incorrect first reasoning steps, as discussed in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Minor perturbation to the correct first step leads to significant loss ‣ 3 Lost at the beginning of reasoning ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. The modified context is highlighted in orange.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>LaBoR benchmark examples</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The self-reflection benchmark includes the following fields: a <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">question</span>, a flawed <span id="A6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">first reason</span>, the <span id="A6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ground truth answer</span>, and the <span id="A6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">source</span> of the original question. The flawed reasoning spans a range of difficulties—from single, easily correctable mistakes (Figure <a href="#A6.F1" title="Figure F.1 ‣ Appendix F LaBoR benchmark examples ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>) to reasoning traces with multiple errors or misleading logic that require deeper revision (Figure <a href="#A6.F2" title="Figure F.2 ‣ Appendix F LaBoR benchmark examples ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="601.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 601.91" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,601.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 596.01 C 0 599.27 2.64 601.91 5.91 601.91 L 471.47 601.91 C 474.73 601.91 477.38 599.27 477.38 596.01 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 580.26 L 475.41 580.26 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 588.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="510.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.91em;">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Example 1 of LaBoR benchmark</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.35em;--ltx-fo-height:40.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="554.68" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 554.68)" width="544.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.35em;">
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Let <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math> be an isosceles trapezoid such that <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD&gt;AB=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD&gt;AB=4</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> be a point on line <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DE=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DE=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be the midpoint of <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{AE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{AE}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given that points <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B,C,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B,C,D</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> lie on a circle with radius <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, compute <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="MD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">MD</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First reason:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Alright, let’s tackle this problem step by step. It’s about an isosceles trapezoid and some points on a circle. Hmm, okay, so let me first parse the information given.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We have an isosceles trapezoid <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD&gt;AB=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD&gt;AB=4</annotation></semantics></math>. So, <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> is one of the bases and it’s 4 units long. Since it’s an isosceles trapezoid, the other base <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> must be longer, which is given. The legs <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math> are equal in length because it’s isosceles.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, point <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is on line <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DE=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DE=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. So, if I imagine the trapezoid, <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> is the longer base. Starting from <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, we go 2 units beyond to point <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ED=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ED=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="A6.F1.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" alttext="EC=CD-ED=CD-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;" mathbackground="#FFCCCC" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EC=CD-ED=CD-2</annotation></semantics></math></span>. But I don’t know <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CDC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CDC</annotation></semantics></math> yet, so maybe I can figure that out later.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Point <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is the midpoint of <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{AE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{AE}</annotation></semantics></math>. So, we connect points <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is halfway along that segment.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given that points <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B,C,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B,C,D</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> lie on a circle with radius 5. So, these five points are concyclic (lie on the same circle), and the circle has a radius of 5. We need to compute <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="MD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">MD</annotation></semantics></math>, the distance from <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Okay, so since <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math> is an isosceles trapezoid, let me recall that in such trapezoids, the legs are equal, and the base angles are equal. Also, the diagonals are equal in length. So, <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC=BD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC=BD</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I think it might help to assign coordinates to the points to make the problem more concrete. Let me try to set up a coordinate system.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let me place the trapezoid so that the bases <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math> are horizontal. Let me let the center of the circle be at the origin, but wait, actually, maybe it’s better to place <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> at a certain position to make calculations easier.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mistakes in first reasoning step:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The <span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;">mistake</span> is the incorrect subtraction of segment lengths. It should be corrected to “<math id="A6.F1.pic1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EC=CD+ED=CD+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EC=CD+ED=CD+2</annotation></semantics></math>” since point <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> lies between <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and the distances should be added, not subtracted.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ground truth answer:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A6.F1.pic1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Source:<span id="A6.F1.pic1.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">HMMT.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure F.1</span>: </span><span id="A6.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example 1 of LaBoR benchmark.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A6.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="767.96" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 767.96" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,767.96) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 762.05 C 0 765.31 2.64 767.96 5.91 767.96 L 471.47 767.96 C 474.73 767.96 477.38 765.31 477.38 762.05 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 746.31 L 475.41 746.31 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 754.36)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="510.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.91em;">
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Example 2 of LaBoR benchmark</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.35em;--ltx-fo-height:52.09em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="720.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 720.72)" width="544.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.35em;">
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Four unit squares form a <math id="A6.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> grid. Each of the 12 unit line segments forming the sides of the squares is colored either red or blue in such a way that each unit square has 2 red sides and 2 blue sides. One example is shown below (red is solid, blue is dashed). Find the number of such colorings.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[asy]
size(4cm);
defaultpen(linewidth(1.2));
draw((0, 0) – (2, 0) – (2, 1));
draw((0, 1) – (1, 1) – (1, 2) – (2,2));
draw((0, 0) – (0, 1), dotted);
draw((1, 0) – (1, 1) – (2, 1) – (2, 2), dotted);
draw((0, 1) – (0, 2) – (1, 2), dotted);
[/asy]</span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First reason:<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Alright, so I have this problem about coloring the sides of a 2x2 grid of squares. Each square has four sides, and each of these sides is colored either red or blue. The condition is that each individual square must have exactly two red sides and two blue sides. The question is asking for the number of such colorings.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">First, let me visualize the grid. It’s a 2x2 grid, so there are four squares arranged in a larger square. Each square has four sides, and <span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;">each side is shared with another square except for the outermost sides</span>. But in the problem, it says there are 12 unit line segments forming the sides of the squares. Wait, let me check that: a 2x2 grid has 3 horizontal lines and 3 vertical lines, each of length 2 units. So, each horizontal line is divided into two segments, right? So, the total number of horizontal segments is 3 rows times 2 segments per row, which is 6, and similarly, the vertical segments are also 3 columns times 2 segments per column, which is another 6. So, 6 + 6 = 12 segments in total. Okay, that makes sense.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each of these 12 segments can be colored either red or blue. However, the constraint is that each of the four squares must have exactly two red sides and two blue sides. So, even though each segment can be colored independently, we have these local constraints for each square.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I think a good way to approach this problem is by considering each square and the possible colorings for its sides, then seeing how they can fit together without violating the constraints. However, since the coloring of one square’s side affects the adjacent squares, this could get complicated.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#CCFFCC;">Maybe I can model this as a graph</span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where each segment is a node, and the squares impose constraints on the nodes (i.e., exactly two red and two blue edges around each square). But I’m not too familiar with graph theory, so maybe that’s not the best approach.</span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Mistakes in first reasoning step:<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFCCCC;">Mistake 1</span> incorrectly assumes that in a <math id="A6.F2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> grid, each corner square has two shared and two unshared sides, without properly accounting for edge distribution. <span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.9.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#CCFFCC;">Mistake 2</span> introduces unnecessary abstraction by treating segments as “nodes,” which obscures the natural structure: the segments themselves are the edges whose colours we choose, and each square simply places a rule on its four incident edges. Working directly with those four constraints is far cleaner than introducing an extra level of abstraction.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Ground truth answer:<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> 82.</span></span></span>
<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Source:<span id="A6.F2.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> AIME25.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure F.2</span>: </span><span id="A6.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example 2 of LaBoR benchmark.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Prompt example for evaluation</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The template for using the DeepSeek-R1 model is provided below. We apply the same structure to other open-source thinking models, with slight adjustments for model-specific input and output formats.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt example for DeepSeek-R1:</span></p><span id="A7.p2.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A7.p2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left">
<span id="A7.p2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|begin_of_sentence|&gt;Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{}.
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.p2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left">
<span id="A7.p2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;|User|&gt;[Question]&lt;|Assistant|&gt;&lt;think&gt;
</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Correlation between first reasoning step and final prediction in Qwen3</h2>

<figure id="A8.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A8.F1.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v1/first_reason_accuracy_qwen3-8b.svg" id="A8.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298"></object>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A8.F1.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v1/first_reason_number_of_tokens_qwen3-8b.svg" id="A8.F1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298"></object>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure H.1</span>: </span><span id="A8.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Accuracy and number of tokens on Qwen3-8B. <span id="A8.F1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> The relationship between the accuracy of the final prediction (<math id="A8.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the correctness of the prediction solely based on the first reasoning step (<math id="A8.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) across different difficulty levels. If <math id="A8.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is incorrect, <math id="A8.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is more likely incorrect. <span id="A8.F1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> The number of tokens used for the final prediction after the first reasoning step <math id="A8.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the number of tokens used for <math id="A8.F1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{2},t_{3},...,t_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{2},t_{3},...,t_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Although <math id="A8.F1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is correct, the model still consumes a large amount of tokens for the following reasoning steps–overthinking.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Closed-source model performance on the LaBoR benchmark</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To better understand models’ performance on self-correction in long-chain-of-thought (CoT) reasoning, we evaluate several closed-source models—OpenAI o4-mini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, Gemini-2.5-Flash-Preview <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>, and Claude-3.7-Sonnet on the LaBoR benchmark.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experimental Setup.</span> Since these closed-source models do not support inserting intermediate reasoning steps directly, we use prompting to simulate the model’s thinking based on the given first reasoning step. The prompts used in our experiments are as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question-only setting:</span></p><span id="A9.p3.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A9.p3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left">
<span id="A9.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Please solve the following math problem step by step. Output only your full thinking process, and then summarize the final answer in \boxed{}.
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A9.p3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left">
<span id="A9.p3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Question: [Question]
</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A9.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question-and-first-reason setting:</span></p><span id="A9.p4.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A9.p4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left">
<span id="A9.p4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Please solve the following math problem step by step. Continue exactly from where you left off, treating the previous reasoning as your own. Build your continued thinking based on it. Output only your full thinking process, and then summarize the final answer in \boxed{}.
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A9.p4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_align_left">
<span id="A9.p4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Question: [Question] 
<br class="ltx_break">Reasoning: [First reason]
</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="A9.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The maximum output token length is set to <math id="A9.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>. We report both model accuracy and the number of generated tokens for each configuration. The results are reported in Figure <a href="#A9.F1" title="Figure I.1 ‣ Appendix I Closed-source model performance on the LaBoR benchmark ‣ Lost at the Beginning of Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I.1</span></a>,</p>
</div>
<figure id="A9.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22058v1/close_model_results.svg" id="A9.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:467/174;" width="467" height="174"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A9.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure I.1</span>: </span><span id="A9.F1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Closed-source model performance on the LaBoR benchmark. <span id="A9.F1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> Accuracy of the final prediction (<math id="A9.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) depending on whether the first reasoning step is included as input. <span id="A9.F1.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> The number of tokens used for the final prediction.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</article>
</div>
